---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Steps from '../../components/Steps.astro'
---
<Base title="Backups - Sanctum guide" description="Take an encrypted backup of your vault, and prove you can restore it before you need to.">
  <section class="section wrap" style="border-top: none;">
    <h2>Backups</h2>
    <p>
      Your vault exists on one machine. A failed drive is the ordinary way to lose it, and there is
      no copy anywhere else unless you make one.
    </p>
    <Steps steps={[
      'Open <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Data</strong>.',
      'Click <strong>Create backup</strong> and choose where to save the <code>.sanctumbak</code> file.',
      'Give the backup its own password. It can differ from your vault passphrase, and it is what protects the file.',
      'Copy the file somewhere off this machine &mdash; another drive, or storage you trust.',
    ]} />
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Prove the restore works</h2>
    <p>
      An untested backup is a guess. The only way to know is to restore one, and the only safe time
      to find out is before you need it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Restoring replaces the current vault entirely, so do it deliberately &mdash; ideally right
      after a fresh backup, when losing the current state costs nothing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>What is in the file</h2>
    <p>
      The whole encrypted database, sealed again under the backup password. Someone holding the file
      without that password gets nothing, and a file that has been altered is refused rather than
      partly trusted.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
